From edeae798c8bb00d0342b4062e1aa20ee8fcfa3c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DoubleGate <parobek@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 23:20:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] [UPSTREAM] notifications: generic webhook sink (JSON, no
 identifiers)

Add an optional `webhook_url`. When set, each notification is POSTed there as
a JSON body `{source, type, message, timestamp}` (Content-Type:
application/json), independently of `ntfy_url`. The payload deliberately
carries no subscriber identifiers (IMSI/IMEI/GUTI) -- only the event type and
the same human-readable message ntfy receives.

Generalizes the notification worker from a single destination to a set of
sinks (ntfy, webhook), each tracked and retried independently by
(notification type, sink): one sink being down no longer re-sends to a healthy
one. ntfy behavior is unchanged when `webhook_url` is unset.

Security:
- `webhook_url` can embed a credential (e.g. a Slack/Discord token in the path),
  so it is redacted from `GET /api/config` and preserved across a config write
  that omits it (empty string clears it).
- `send_notification` strips the URL from any transport error before it is
  returned, so the destination (a private ntfy topic is itself a secret) cannot
  leak into the daemon log.

Tests: webhook JSON body + Content-Type, both-sinks delivery, webhook_url
redaction, and the preserve/clear/replace resolver.

Ref: Orbic-Rayhunter T-OR-047.
Signed-off-by: DoubleGate <parobek@gmail.com>
